[{"id":"VRCE-1-10-1","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":10,"verse":1,"english":"And he said again, O foremost of monarchs, do you listen to me as I relate how that intelligent Sanatkumāra, best of deities, spoke.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.615,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-11-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1010001","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9deb9e856fa8fafdec95d0a27984cb012afd7ed3114224f56937a092bb922e13","compact":"70628f0ce558ea437d374ea19ad13e9dd2a6fa89b1ec117353f98f7fdc798b54","nasal":"de018cf547a4c95fbec6bd8eaebd8b1070cc0ee6403d02051b1e09fe9c2b974a"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-10-2","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":10,"verse":2,"english":"In the line of Ikşvāku will be born a righteous king, named Dasaratha, fair of form, and firm in promise.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.691,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-11-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1010002","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7c7254d370cc107df8060a8d27e74a8516a103d58950619a6bd55930ea98b1cf","compact":"e9f1df0a038749c080e0d020678294d8b77e2c9de9678e2543a36f2dd6e2c6ac","nasal":"e9f1df0a038749c080e0d020678294d8b77e2c9de9678e2543a36f2dd6e2c6ac"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-10-3","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":10,"verse":3,"english":"That king will contract friendship with the ruler of the Angas. And the latter will have a highly pious daughter, śāntā by name. And the (old) king of the Angas will have a son, named Romapāda. And repairing to him, the highly famous king Dasaratha will speak to Romapada, O righteous-souled one! I am without issue. Let śāntā's husband, desired by you, take charge of this sacrifice of mine, to be celebrated with the object of my obtaining a son to perpetuate the race.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-11-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1010003","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5ce66837897d3fd5509db4276c7400d90dc04cf38ac24fa4a600b87ec20a2a5a","compact":"fe8fae8d193d5947b0d089d6542771ee6ea2c805bf389cd438a82c609ff76f98","nasal":"801a846aeaa3f842d761679f5b058f46858a588921c76ca4b9e81f232cc5f5e4"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-10-4","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":10,"verse":4,"english":"That king will contract friendship with the ruler of the Angas. And the latter will have a highly pious daughter, śāntā by name. And the (old) king of the Angas will have a son, named Romapāda. And repairing to him, the highly famous king Dasaratha will speak to Romapada, O righteous-souled one! I am without issue. Let śāntā's husband, desired by you, take charge of this sacrifice of mine, to be celebrated with the object of my obtaining a son to perpetuate the race.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.883,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-11-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1010004","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"080b66892bdb642c2a862c44e5a44b3365c0726bc6d415550d099181bca3e503","compact":"a56f2b0293a03901d1599e94cf05b469c9fdf972a10ed3bc268458570d69ae3a","nasal":"f6d99649ae2e4e4ea7d203a9300d99f6e067926a70314f990347247a9b17382c"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-10-5","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":10,"verse":5,"english":"That king will contract friendship with the ruler of the Angas. And the latter will have a highly pious daughter, śāntā by name. And the (old) king of the Angas will have a son, named Romapāda. And repairing to him, the highly famous king Dasaratha will speak to Romapada, O righteous-souled one! I am without issue. Let śāntā's husband, desired by you, take charge of this sacrifice of mine, to be celebrated with the object of my obtaining a son to perpetuate the race.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.647,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-11-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1010005","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0d8ce03500cb3ea9032b040b8f7321a14c8f8e36f889fe464aa0b56258232511","compact":"6becdf72f8118c47a1b37ba6b832d90357fc0e167a38c1e249472422bfbc15e4","nasal":"dd2aad0669203642acc69af4f5831e11f1dc299f9370362612eae546a4e3aef9"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-10-6","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":10,"verse":6,"english":"Hearing these words of the king, and having pondered well, he will make over to him Rsyasînga of subdued senses, together with Santa and his children.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-11-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1010006","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ae47ccbf04a9d9667113f04433c4e068433d0139e9d2265011eed8c21664cd53","compact":"fb3db93cba0fd3498aefc80baa586ad861b76cf4dfda84a552bc3238c68f4405","nasal":"ecfd01861d5f668bc694d32d7d3920ed248c6fac7f6660cccaca62489757f0d4"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-10-7","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":10,"verse":7,"english":"And taking that Vipra, that king, his mind free from anxiety, with a glad heart, will prepare for that sacrifice.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-11-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1010007","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5f9197f7e33777d620da1d3393cee8e037b53fa07ee10ca1fd955d30b174c39e","compact":"8d4c0249356797224f8c1b6a9180184d23d82e9d5a40f266c5f65af9acaeff92","nasal":"3ac0c500bb492972a5871bf9ee46d596c7dbeae69b3b67ad15b5c88941e2a6e7"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-10-8","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":10,"verse":8,"english":"And king Dasaratha, knowing duty and desirous of fame, with the intention of obtaining offspring and heaven, with folded hands, will appoint that best of Brahmanas, Rsyasriga, to conduct the ceremony. And that bringer of good will attain his object at the hands of that foremost of Brāhmaṇas.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.578,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-11-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1010008","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8a07c4b02d2c0d9d8113a67bc3ec042785148519cf0af95e56f791f02a38d4f5","compact":"b28ea35d72b06a3b2197e7818152f554e9de8aa41e2809076ad08492b2003246","nasal":"e5b9c95e1e4642479908f81c9d9d275da3890008eb38f75e140d479439a598ff"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-10-9","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":10,"verse":9,"english":"And king Dasaratha, knowing duty and desirous of fame, with the intention of obtaining offspring and heaven, with folded hands, will appoint that best of Brahmanas, Rsyasriga, to conduct the ceremony. And that bringer of good will attain his object at the hands of that foremost of Brāhmaṇas.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-11-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1010009","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e288cadc7121fc5048fabd0794f292bdb5239d355c1e89162038c17abb399d95","compact":"2648c7712dc1e08949b3b6d4eb52054f2bf142ae9f97756406d9b7a24590a358","nasal":"2648c7712dc1e08949b3b6d4eb52054f2bf142ae9f97756406d9b7a24590a358"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-10-10","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":10,"verse":10,"english":"And four sons will be born to him of immeasurable prowess, bringing fame to the family, and known by all.' Thus spoke formerly in the divine age, that worshipful and foremost of deities, Sanatkumāra.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-11-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1010010","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1e363aad219285ece923fd999bb15c397fd6d458960b2dc2d662c81f729c4cc1","compact":"965bfddc289ca710009c6323cba40fd7b081e2f4e1edee9da1b07423c6591445","nasal":"8bf41497501cc02a7109bb98fa1b6e52cd855139193799535478e50d9de59b81"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-10-11","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":10,"verse":11,"english":"And four sons will be born to him of immeasurable prowess, bringing fame to the family, and known by all.' Thus spoke formerly in the divine age, that worshipful and foremost of deities, Sanatkumāra.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-11-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1010011","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7f3a2d3f7b8d090feda6c0a026c00c1d8e06b8c41f28c4569321cdd17a2313b7","compact":"b108a909fc3a605ee900e1f4f389cb8f26962e80ee8833edba78a8c4fb39af8a","nasal":"b108a909fc3a605ee900e1f4f389cb8f26962e80ee8833edba78a8c4fb39af8a"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-10-12","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":10,"verse":12,"english":"Therefore, do you, O tiger among men, repairing there, accompanied with your forces and equipage, yourself, O mighty king, bring Rşyasſrga over with due honours.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.843,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-11-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1010012","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ab9bd521770b4763ab7d4aac185ded611e8b31de82be866bfc72b2631ce3ee00","compact":"312a4782745c17942f09cc2fa12cd2e9d76e8f547d1c6c1fa24da02f1841a137","nasal":"312a4782745c17942f09cc2fa12cd2e9d76e8f547d1c6c1fa24da02f1841a137"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-10-13","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":10,"verse":13,"english":"Hearing Sumantra's words, Dasaratha was exceedingly delighted. And hearing these words, and permitted by Vasistha, he, accompanied with the ladies, and his courtiers, set out for the place where that twice-born one was.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.885,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-11-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1010013","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b0376e65001868a481fabf4bd1cf8688e4a4a4461bf19073f1719e25d34b121b","compact":"c8f854f26fcd1b7a147953b2cdf3297aad42b74ebc7f0dc1eedf67b59eef2e6d","nasal":"5064684f2396e4c9942a4d33107ddd8873bd62ffbe67825141f71c29e5954598"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-10-14","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":10,"verse":14,"english":"And gradually passing by woods and fells, he arrived at the place where that foremost of ascetics was.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.754,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-11-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1010014","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f8375868933ff86e9b944c217d0ecfc223fec61e9dcaeb9ac063444353bf6074","compact":"2ddbde929de08845363d99b2dbbd3747efcb2b1a27cfe938f40c5bf56d69b5d5","nasal":"2ddbde929de08845363d99b2dbbd3747efcb2b1a27cfe938f40c5bf56d69b5d5"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-10-15","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":10,"verse":15,"english":"And coming before that best of regenerate ones, he saw that sage's son near Romapāda, like that of a flaming fire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.717,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-11-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1010015","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b334723b9c89546540747111bdaaf41eac9dba34e255d1efe14bccdfc47a7cc8","compact":"0f5d4024a2f4d9829129a88630ab5d57055db5bed05ce09e5365243edc76fc26","nasal":"0f5d4024a2f4d9829129a88630ab5d57055db5b