,"alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-11-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1010018","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"be8948409c2b69e18664cc3244a6fc5d0072d338d7a29a7dcc724c22ad6fbd42","compact":"bb41b50df525ca2c327658e791fb9e6ae0f82479b1e62cb7ab00fc70d4f29a22","nasal":"bb41b50df525ca2c327658e791fb9e6ae0f82479b1e62cb7ab00fc70d4f29a22"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-10-19","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":10,"verse":19,"english":"Having passed seven or eight days with Romapäda, receiving high honours, that foremost of men, Dasaratha spoke to Romapada,. saying, Let your daughter, O king, together with her husband, O lord of men, repair to my city. I am going to be engaged in a mighty enterprise.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.695,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-11-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1010019","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"40c66942b14783bc0dad203daa81cb7762c7772e6be605c6fde79292548d7da5","compact":"2976cfff6fbc377d999c644bd52430fa63126e627ac099efdfd7a7ffc0c67b53","nasal":"83064477defa177aa463cd5949c41d2646e0d60f685b51e1dc98dfa0fa05e1cf"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-10-20","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":10,"verse":20,"english":"Hearing this as to the journey of that intelligent one, the king said to that Vipra, Do you repair with your wife! Thereupon the saint's son, promising to go, said to the king, So be it!","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-11-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1010020","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b96439c1d12e103fa891205377574920a081217a0a4f3c72c05d54d707fd9969","compact":"f5d6d80d26d29a7b3804dd0bf4ab05d2d62a3efec1be8337600fcf5f6f7a3ae8","nasal":"f5d6d80d26d29a7b3804dd0bf4ab05d2d62a3efec1be8337600fcf5f6f7a3ae8"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-10-21","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":10,"verse":21,"english":"Hearing this as to the journey of that intelligent one, the king said to that Vipra, Do you repair with your wife! Thereupon the saint's son, promising to go, said to the king, So be it! Then with the king's permission, he set out with his wife. Dasaratha and the puissant Romapāda clasping each other by the palm, and embracing each other in affection, attained excess. of joy. Then Raghu's son, bidding farewell to his friend, set out.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.5,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-11-14","DUTT-1-11-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1010021","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e19532d09b25edd97e70c67ace7e6dd5f0d2a3c3f28816502f118cc939ab4f45","compact":"e2ca21eb4427f4146a7a179461faeba9357432d4a514b6a96b065e91bc5030ba","nasal":"e2ca21eb4427f4146a7a179461faeba9357432d4a514b6a96b065e91bc5030ba"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-10-22","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":10,"verse":22,"english":"Then with the king's permission, he set out with his wife. Dasaratha and the puissant Romapāda clasping each other by the palm, and embracing each other in affection, attained excess. of joy. Then Raghu's son, bidding farewell to his friend, set out.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.886,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-11-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1010022","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c3e782c7483eead9c802d71baff3654d2ddb2e58d9a3f311601d8759b4ed0d28","compact":"20c088531a151bd216ef21184a5bfdc980c9aef42af22809a24e731e03ae601e","nasal":"01b0aa41db00e5f5dd8617ea348415172e5bf28e7494e1d53be23e49ec29187d"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-10-23","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":10,"ver